@@ -30,6 +30,8 @@ The plugin adds the following attributes defined at node level:
     * **to_zone** (id, mandatory) -- Policy Destination Zone
     * **action** (string, mandatory, one of `permit`, `deny`) -- Policy Action
 
+* **firewall.zonebased.rules** (list, same item format as **default_rules**) -- specific zone to zone rules. **Only PAN-OS renders it.** On FortiOS, vSRX and VyOS the attribute is accepted and silently has no effect; the platform fork warns (turn the warning off with **defaults.firewall.zonebased.warnings.rules_not_rendered: False**). Use **firewall.policy.rules** ([](plugin-firewall-policy)) for specific rules on FortiOS.
+
 Additional interface level attributes:
 * **firewall.zone** (id) -- the firewall zone for this firewall interface
 
